MWO-LTSA-064 |
DONE |
Reporting implemented for LTSA Demo v1, per the Product Owner's
manager-first priority order. New ReportsWorkspace.jsx (mirrors
LTSAWorkspace's own internal Tabs pattern) hosts five reports, wired
into LTSAWorkspace.jsx as a seventh tab ("Reports"): (1) Executive
Summary Report reuses KpiCardGrid/MaintenanceHealthPanel/
AttentionAssetList/UpcomingMaintenanceList and their existing
executiveDashboard.js data functions verbatim (MWO-LTSA-063); (2) Pump
History Report reuses AssetSummaryCard + buildAssetSummary/
buildAssetTimeline/listAssets (MWO-LTSA-062) across every pump; (3-5)
Work Order/Preventive Maintenance/Corrective Maintenance Reports each
directly reuse the existing WorkOrderRegistryTable/PMScheduleTable/
CMReportTable components read-only (selectedId=null, no-op onSelect)
— no new table markup written for any of the three. Two small new
shared components: PrintButton.jsx (window.print(), the browser's
"Save as PDF" capability — no PDF library) and ReportGeneratedOn.jsx
(date stamp). Print styling (Reports.css) uses an opt-out .no-print
class plus @page{size:A4} rather than the common "hide everything in
body, reveal one subtree" trick — the latter was considered and
rejected because it leaks globally once bundled and would blank out
printing on every other page in the app that happens to load the
stylesheet (all component CSS is bundled globally, not scoped to
which tab is active). LTSAWorkspace's own outer Tabs bar was also
marked .no-print so it doesn't appear in printed reports; App.jsx
(Dashboard shell) was not touched — this MWO's scope did not extend
there, so the outermost OS/LTSA section-switcher tabs will still
appear at the top of a printed page as a known, documented, in-scope
limitation. Five ReportsWorkspace tab labels use full report names
("Work Order Report", not "Work Order") to avoid duplicate tab labels
with LTSAWorkspace's own outer tabs, which are both mounted
simultaneously whenever Reports is the active outer tab. No
PM/CM/WO/Pump component, page, or sample data file was modified; no
chart library or other external dependency introduced.

