FLAT badge comparing the two most recent weeks' corrective-maintenance
counts (rising reactive work = the clearest "getting worse" signal
available) — a table, not a chart; "What should managers do next?"
via a new RecommendedActionsList, driven by
buildRecommendedActions() — conditional, data-driven bullets (e.g.
"Schedule N overdue PM tasks") each carrying the real count it was
derived from, never static text. REFERENCE_DATE and
daysBeforeReference() were exported from executiveDashboard.js
(previously private) so analytics.js anchors "today" identically
instead of duplicating the constant — confirmed behavior-preserving
via existing executiveDashboard tests, unchanged. No chart library;
only Card/Badge/EmptyState/PageHeader plus existing LTSA components
reused. No PM/CM/WO/Pump component, page, or sample data file was
