bars, detail panels, empty states, responsive CSS breakpoints,
keyboard row activation, print CSS) before changing anything. Fixed
three concrete gaps found: (1) QuickNavigationPanel had not been
updated when MWO-064/065 added the Reports and Analytics tabs, so
those two workspaces were unreachable from the Executive Dashboard's
navigation shortcuts — added "Open Reports"/"Open Analytics" using
the existing onNavigate mechanism, no new navigation pattern
introduced. (2) Pump Detail's "View History" Quick Action button had
been permanently disabled since MWO-060 (written before the
Maintenance History/Asset 360 tab existed); now that the tab exists
(MWO-062), the button was a dead end a first-time user could click
with no effect and no explanation — enabled it and wired it to
onNavigate("history"), the same tab-switch mechanism already used by
QuickNavigationPanel and passed to every LTSAWorkspace page. Threaded
onNavigate from LTSAWorkspace -> Pump -> PumpDetailPanel; optional
chaining keeps Pump usable standalone without the prop. "Documents"
remains disabled — no equivalent feature exists anywhere to link to,
so leaving it disabled is correct, not a gap. (3) The four oldest
FilterBars (Pump/Work Order/PM/CM, from MWO-056-059) had a raw status
<select> with no accessible name, inconsistent with the labelled
pattern MaintenanceHistoryFilterBar (MWO-062) already established for
its own selects — added aria-label="Filter by status" to each,
visual layout unchanged. Every other audited area (empty-state
messages, no-selection panels, horizontal-scroll wrapping, keyboard
Enter/Space row activation, responsive breakpoints, print CSS,
terminology) was already consistent from the prior progressive polish
MWOs (056, 060, 062-065) and needed no change — not padded with
unnecessary edits. No backend/API, architecture, business-logic, or
design-system file touched; sample data files untouched.

